// Issue #2350, `docs/decision-log.md` 2026-08-07 "Cue/parenthetical tag
// extensions: strip-then-match, uniformly" — the #2077 heading rule
// (slug/tag structure stripped before matching, rather than declining the
// whole line) widened to `CUE`/`PARENTHETICAL` too.
//
// Before this issue, `hir::lower_native::element::candidate`'s literalness
// rule declined a `CUE`/`PARENTHETICAL` carrying a trailing tag extension
// outright (§8d.4, `@VENDOR #(v.o.)`) — this exact fixture would have
// failed to compile with two `E129`s, one per claimed line below. Both
// handlers are plain `claims` (no `attach`), so — unlike the built-in
// screenplay preset's attach-mode `cue`/`parenthetical`
// (`tests/tier1-native/conventions-screenplay-preset`), which still
// declines a tag-bearing line under the *separate* "attach mode has
// nowhere to carry a claim's tags" rule — these claim and lower to a call
// exactly as their untagged counterparts already did.
//
// The tag's own text isn't observable in `run_native_transcript`'s output
// (`Step::Line`'s `tags` field is dropped by that helper — only the
// printed prose is, the same limitation `inline-tag-embedded-brace`'s own
// doc names); `crates/internal/brink-ir/src/hir/lower_native/tests.rs`'s
// `a_cue_with_a_tag_extension_is_now_claimable` and
// `a_parenthetical_with_a_tag_extension_is_now_claimable` assert the tag
// actually reaches `Content.tags` directly. This fixture's signal is
// narrower but end-to-end: a tag-carrying cue/parenthetical compiles and
// runs at all, claimed rather than falling through to a loud `E129`, and
// the pattern still sees only the name/delivery text — the tag is
// stripped, not appended or otherwise leaked into the captured payload.

@[convention(claims = "^(?<name>[A-Z][A-Z ]*)$", order = 10)]
fn cue(name: string) {
  return name;
}

@[convention(claims = "^(?<delivery>[a-z][a-z' -]*)$", order = 20)]
fn parenthetical(delivery: string) {
  return delivery;
}

flow main() {
  @VENDOR #(v.o.)
  (hushed) #whisper
  You shouldn't be here after dark.
  -> END
}
